# DTF tier manifest: virtual-member-gates
#   (artifact-keeper#4098/#4343, #4286, #4346; all fixed in 1.11.0)
# Profile-set: filesystem / single + upstreams=mock-npm (a stdlib-python npm
# registry serving `dtf-held` 1.0.0 under any path prefix at 172.16.<slot>.90,
# logging every request).
#
# A virtual repository must apply each member's own gates: a caller must not
# reach THROUGH the virtual what the member itself would refuse. This tier is
# about the member gates; virtual-usage (aggregation + member editability)
# and virtual-no-transfer / nexus-group-virtual (migration) are not repeated.
#
# THE BUGS
# #4098/#4343  quarantine hold: a scan-on-proxy npm (PyPI, VS Code) virtual
#        walked past a member that answered 409 (quarantine hold) and served
#        the very tarball from the next member. Fixed: the hold is final.
# #4286  scan policy: the npm virtual tarball path discarded the gated
#        lookup's 403/409 and served the row its `{pkg}/%/{file}` pattern
#        lookup found, so a hosted tarball a `block_unscanned` policy refuses
#        was served through any virtual over that hosted repository. Same
#        class in Maven: the virtual member closure swallowed the refusal, and
#        a `-SNAPSHOT` alias resolved to its timestamped jar with no download
#        gate at all (direct and through a virtual).
# #4346  visibility: RPM virtual repodata (repomd.xml, primary.xml.gz) was
#        built from EVERY member, so an anonymous caller of a public virtual
#        read the names/versions/digests of a private member's packages. Also,
#        attaching an `internal` repository as a member now needs a read grant
#        (a delegated virtual admin could otherwise re-export it).
#
# RED image: ak-backend:1.10.0. GREEN: 1.11.0 and later. On 1.10.0 the
# `internal` visibility does not exist yet, so the attach case is red there
# because the repository cannot be made internal; its refusal body is asserted
# on green.
#
# RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED=false: one admin login, a second user, ~50 API calls back
# to back. UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS=true: the npm remotes' upstream is the
# mock on a private address (the profile also sets it).
PROFILES="storage.filesystem upstreams.mock-npm"
ORACLE="oracle.sh"
RATE_LIMIT_ENABLED="false"
UPSTREAM_ALLOW_PRIVATE_IPS="true"
